description:
In repos/activity-api/src/routes/activities.ts, add a new "liveness" conservation invariant to the GET /conservation-audit handler.

ANCHOR. Ground on this line, which occurs EXACTLY ONCE in the file:
    if (want('memory')) {

Insert the new block on the lines IMMEDIATELY BEFORE that line, at the same indentation, inside the same try block. Do not modify the memory invariant or anything else.

ONE OPERATION. Insert this block verbatim:

    if (want('liveness')) {
      // LIVENESS — a lane that STOPS emitting while the fleet keeps working is a
      // silent break. Measured as SHARE of recent executions, never a raw count,
      // so an idle substrate does not read as a broken one. No datetime WHERE
      // anywhere: on this store a datetime conjunct silently drops its partner
      // predicate, so the window is cut client-side from an ordered fetch.
      const recentRows = await surrealDB.query<Record<string, unknown>>(
        'SELECT activity_id FROM execution ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 2000'
      );
      const rows = recentRows ?? [];
      if (rows.length >= 800) {
        const newest = rows.slice(0, 500);
        const prior = rows.slice(500);
        const shareIn = (set: Array<Record<string, unknown>>, id: string): number =>
          set.length === 0 ? 0 : set.filter((r) => String(r['activity_id']) === id).length / set.length;
        const priorIds = new Set(prior.map((r) => String(r['activity_id'])));
        for (const id of priorIds) {
          const before = shareIn(prior, id);
          if (before < 0.01) continue;
          const after = shareIn(newest, id);
          if (after < before * 0.25) {
            violations.push({ invariant: 'liveness', activity_id: id, prior_share: Number(before.toFixed(4)), recent_share: Number(after.toFixed(4)), note: 'lane emission share collapsed while the fleet kept executing - the lane is silently broken, not merely idle' });
          }
        }
      }
    }

WHY THIS IS NEEDED, and why it is not redundant with the existing checks. On 2026-09-07 a substrate-authored commit truncated the compose trace emitter, so feature_compose stopped writing execution rows for over an hour while the rest of the fleet kept executing normally. Nothing detected it. Measured shares across that outage: feature_compose held 14 of 383 fleet executions before (3.7%), fell to 2 of 309 during (0.6%), and recovered to 7 of 316 after (2.2%) — a collapse against a stable denominator. The existing `addressing` invariant cannot catch this because it is a ratio over ALL history and moves far too slowly to register a one-hour outage. This check is deliberately relative, so it fires on a lane going dark rather than on the substrate being quiet.

The variable `violations` already exists in this handler's scope and is the array the other invariants push into. `surrealDB.query` is already used by every other invariant in this same handler; follow that exact call style.

